From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:54:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sched/features: Enable MISFIT_RUNTIME

On the M4 MacBook Pro the equal-slice 10-thread memory bandwidth test
reaches macOS's figure only when the E core slices move to the P cores
that finish first. Turn MISFIT_RUNTIME on by default; it can still be
switched off at runtime with NO_MISFIT_RUNTIME in
/sys/kernel/debug/sched/features.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 kernel/sched/features.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/features.h b/kernel/sched/features.h
index a18c5e10d3..26f53ceb34 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/features.h
+++ b/kernel/sched/features.h
@@ -147,7 +147,7 @@ SCHED_FEAT(MISFIT_ROTATE, true)
  * sleeping for misfit_runtime_ns on a CPU smaller than it may use as a
  * misfit, before its PELT utilization has grown past the smaller CPU.
  */
-SCHED_FEAT(MISFIT_RUNTIME, false)
+SCHED_FEAT(MISFIT_RUNTIME, true)
 
 SCHED_FEAT(LATENCY_WARN, false)
 
-- 
2.43.0

